---
description: The Adventures of Tom, always-on project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` first, then only the docs the task needs (`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/CANON.md`, `docs/BATTLE_SYSTEM.md`, `docs/WORKFLOW.md`).

- The owner (Tom) does not code. You do all technical work. Do not ask him to run commands, edit files or choose between implementations. Make the call and say which one in a line. Ask only when a choice cannot be undone, and then one short question.
- Reply in a few plain sentences. Tables beat prose. No flourish. Define any technical term you use.
- No em dashes in anything you write for Tom or put in the game.
- Plain browser JavaScript, classic scripts in one global scope, no modules, no bundler, no build step. Load order is the `<script>` order in `index.html`.
- Phone first (portrait), landscape toggle must keep working.
- Before you finish: `python3 tools/smoke.py` must exit 0 and you must look at the screenshots in `tools/shots/`.
- Do not reword spoken lines (baked audio matches exact text). Do not touch `data/voice-clips.js` or `data/voice/*.js`.
- Work on a branch. Small commits. Finish by listing the exact files you changed.
